You are a senior Android engineer, backend engineer, cloud streaming engineer, UI/UX designer, DevOps engineer, security engineer, and SaaS architect.

I want you to build a professional, production-ready Android application for multi-platform live streaming.

IMPORTANT:
Do not create only a UI prototype.
Do not create fake buttons that do nothing.
Do not use mock streaming functionality where a real implementation is technically possible.
Build the application with a scalable architecture and clearly separate Android frontend, backend API, database, cloud storage, streaming workers, payment system, and admin panel.

If an external service requires API keys, OAuth credentials, payment credentials, developer approval, RTMP credentials, cloud credentials, or server configuration, create the complete integration structure and clearly identify the required configuration values. Never expose secret credentials inside the Android APK.

==================================================
1. APP PURPOSE
==================================================

Build an Android application that allows users to:

1. Stream live to YouTube.
2. Stream live to Facebook.
3. Stream live to TikTok where official API/account permissions allow.
4. Support Telegram-compatible streaming workflows where officially supported.
5. Stream to custom RTMP/RTMPS destinations.
6. Stream from the phone camera.
7. Stream the Android screen.
8. Stream microphone audio.
9. Stream device audio where Android/device permissions allow.
10. Add camera overlay while screen sharing.
11. Upload prerecorded videos.
12. Stream prerecorded videos to supported destinations.
13. Loop prerecorded videos.
14. Schedule prerecorded streams.
15. Run cloud-based prerecorded streams after the Android app is closed.
16. Support continuous cloud streaming for up to 7 days for eligible paid users.
17. Support 16:9 landscape streaming.
18. Support 9:16 portrait streaming.
19. Support resolutions up to 4K where the device, encoder, server, and destination support it.
20. Support 30 FPS and 60 FPS reliably.
21. Only expose higher FPS options when technically supported by the destination.
22. Provide stream health monitoring.
23. Provide automatic reconnect.
24. Provide stream history.
25. Provide analytics.
26. Provide subscriptions.
27. Provide payment management.
28. Provide a complete admin dashboard.
